```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Display Background Image</title>
    <style>
        body {
            text-align: center;
        }

        button {
            background-color: #4CAF50;
            color: white;
            padding: 10px 20px;
            border: none;
            cursor: pointer;
        }

        button:hover {
            background-color: #45a049;
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <h1>Display Background Image</h1>
    <button onclick="displayBackgroundImage()">Display Background Image</button>

    <script>
        function displayBackgroundImage() {
            const img = document.createElement('img');
            img.src = chrome.runtime.getURL('background.jpg'); // Replace 'background.jpg' with the actual path to your background image.
            img.onload = function () {
                chrome.tabs.query({ active: true, currentWindow: true }, tabs => {
                    chrome.tabs.executeScript(tabs[0].id, { file: 'content.js' });
                });
            };
        }
    </script>
</body>
</html>
```

Make sure to replace `'background.jpg'` with the actual path to your background image. Also, you need to create two files named `content.js` and `background.jpg` in the same directory as the HTML file. The `content.js` file will contain the code to set the background image:

```javascript
document.body.style.backgroundImage = "url(" + chrome.extension.getURL('background.jpg') + ")";
```

And the `background.jpg` file will be the image you want to set as the background.

